    "ml1150: RAM for the swap tier that is not counted against Madeira's limit, donated by the MadeiraMemoryHost extension (512 MB regions, created untouched, handed over, then the extension exits). With swap-mb it is the swap tier's first stage, taken before the swap file; without swap-mb it is the only stage (ml2200 donor-only, madeira.cfg donor-only = 0 turns that off) and what it cannot cover stays normal app memory. Taken while free RAM stays above MADEIRA_DONOR_POOL_MARGIN_MB and iOS reports no memory pressure. Off by default; read at launch.": {
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "由辅助扩展提供、不计入主应用上限的内存，按 512 MB 区域交付。"
          }
        }
      },
      "extractionState": "manual"
    },
    "ml1150: the donor pool takes no more memory while the host's free RAM is below this many MB. Off (0) since ml2021: iOS keeps free RAM low on purpose, so 1024 and then 256 refused most takes on device; the memory-pressure notification alone guards. Set 256 to restore the old floor.": {
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "宿主空闲内存低于指定 MB 时不再申请，0 关闭此限制。"
          }
        }
      },
      "extractionState": "manual"
    },
    "ml1150: the old lifetime count penalized an asynchronous culling loop after its third check, even if those checks were a frame apart. Keep cooperative back-pressure for tight polling only. A 250us gap starts a new burst; completed querie...": {
