    },
    "ml2021: the stage a 64-bit program's memory takes first; the other is the fallback. Unset: the swap file while a 32-bit program is in the session (a guest window held or in use), so the kernel can evict the launcher chain's idle pages and the donor pool stays for the 32-bit program, which may not use the file; donor RAM first otherwise. 1: donor RAM first, always (the old behaviour). 2: the swap file first, always.": {
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
