      "extractionState": "manual"
    },
    "ml2021: what the tier may do with memory a 32-bit program commits (inside its WoW64 guest window). Unset: donor RAM only, the memory stays ordinary RAM when the pool has none; it never goes to the swap file, which paged a 32-bit title's heap in and out of flash and froze it for seconds at a time. 1: donor RAM, then the swap file, like 64-bit programs (the old behaviour). 2: never tiered. The 64-bit launcher and helpers next to it still use the pool and the file.": {
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
