    "ml2240: on (default): a 64-bit exe or DLL without relocations whose base lies between 4 GB and the start of the app's address space (an old x64 linker's default 0x100000000, which iOS never maps) is mapped elsewhere, its header names the real base, and its own preferred-base addresses are served by the fault handler and FEX, as below 4 GB. The range is used only when a fixed allocation at its first and last page is refused as outside the map. Before, such an image failed to start (c0000018; log 115: the DirectX redistributable's x64 installer helper, so a game's first-run install script stopped). 0: the 4 GB limit, as before.": {
