    },
    "ml2290: on (default): a thread that exits frees the previous exited thread's stacks only after finding that thread, by its process, thread id and pthread, in the live TEB list (the hand-off env.MADEIRA_EA_CEF = 1 already used). 32-bit processes started one after another can get the same window and TEB addresses; the unchecked hand-off then made a new thread free its own kernel stack at exit and hang there holding the memory lock (testers' log, 2026-10-31: a launcher installer's second VC++ redistributable, the installer waiting on that thread forever). 0: the upstream hand-off, unless MADEIRA_EA_CEF = 1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "核实进程、线程 ID 和实时线程记录后再释放旧线程栈。"
          }
        }
      },
      "extractionState": "manual"
    },
    "ml2310: off (default): a game from another store (an Epic library entry) starts without the fixed Steam identity (SteamAppId, SteamGameId, SteamAppPath) every other launch outside Madeira Dock gets. With it, a game's launcher took its Steam path, its Steam API start failed and it showed only an error (testers' log, 2026-10-31: a publisher's launcher started by an Epic copy, 'Steam failed to initialize'). 1: publishes it as before.": {
      "localizations": {
